  "text": "כספי relentlessly enforces himself studies persistently online\n\n])){\nccording to the problem, we need to find the value of\n\\[\\frac{1}{a_1a_2}+\\frac{1}{a_2a_3}+\\dots+\\frac{1}{a_na_1}.\\]\n\nDefine $S = \\frac{1}{a_1a_2}+\\frac{1}{a_2a_3}+\\dots+\\frac{1}{a_na_1}$.\n\nNow, let's multiply $S$ by $\\frac{1}{a_1a_2}$. We get\n\\[S\\cdot\\frac{1}{a_1a_2} = \\frac{1}{a_2}+\\frac{1}{a_3}+\\dots+\\frac{1}{a_{n-1}}+\\frac{1}{a_n}.\\]\nNext, let's multiply $S$ by $\\frac{1}{a_2a_3}$. We get\n\\[S\\cdot\\frac{1}{a_2a_3} = \\frac{1}{a_3}+\\frac{1}{a_4}+\\dots+\\frac{1}{a_n}+\\frac{1}{a_1}.\\]\nAnd so on, we can multiply $S$ by $\\frac{1}{a_ka_{k+1}}$, and we will get\n\\[S\\cdot\\frac{1}{a_{k}a_{k+1}} = \\frac{1}{a_{k+1}}+\\frac{1}{a_{k+2}}+\\dots+\\frac{1}{a_n}+\\frac{1}{a_1}.\\]\n\nNow, if we add all these equations, we get\n\\[S\\left(\\frac{1}{a_1}+\\frac{1}{a_2}+\\dots+\\frac{1}{a_n}\\right) = n\\left(\\frac{1}{a_1}+\\frac{1}{a_2}+\\dots+\\frac{1}{a_n}\\right).\\]\n\nThis means that\n\\[S\\left(\\frac{1}{a_1}+\\frac{1}{a_2}+\\dots+\\frac{1}{a_n}\\right) = n\\left(\\frac{1}{a_1}+\\frac{1}{a_2}+\\dots+\\frac{1}{a_n}\\right).\\]\n\nSince $a_1,a_2,\\dots, a_n$ are non-zero complex numbers, we can divide both sides by $\\left(\\frac{1}{a_1}+\\frac{1}{a_2}+\\dots+\\frac{1}{a_n}\\right)$ to get\n\\[S = n.\\]\n\nNext, let's divide both sides by $\\left(\\frac{1}{a_1}+\\frac{1}{a_2}+\\dots+\\frac{1}{a_n}\\right)$, we get\n\\[S = n.\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of\n\\[\\frac{1}{a_1a_2}+\\frac{1}{a_2a_3}+\\dots+\\frac{1}{a_na_1}\\]is\n\\[\\boxed{n}.\\]",
